## Flow Convention And Cache

`warp_with_support` / `warp_disp` use backward grid sampling:

```text
output(p) = source(p + flow(p))
```

To warp `t-1` into `t`, cache must store target-to-source flow:

```text
warp_flow[t-1] = RAFT(frame_t -> frame_t-1)
```

`build_aux_cache.py` implements this convention. Existing aux cache files contain:

```text
rgb:       uint8, shape [T, 256, 320, 3]
warp_flow: float16, shape [T-1, 2, 256, 320]
occ:       uint8, shape [T-1, 256, 320]
```

Aux cache size: approximately `7.9G`.

## Mask Convention

Training warp loss uses:

- current validity;
- warped previous validity;
- in-bounds sampling support;
- target-frame occlusion from cached `occ`;
- finite/border-safe sampling region.

It does not intersect with unwarped previous validity.

